"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[41862],{41862:e=>{e.exports="# LOD Migration Guide\n\n## Status: Partially Supported (~40-55% of LOD expressions migratable)\n\n## Mechanisms\n\nClassify each LOD calculation, then apply the matching mechanism:\n\n| LOD Type             | Mechanism         | What to Do                                             |\n| -------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| FIXED / TABLE_SCOPED | `SOURCE_SQL_OVER` | Add `AGG(expr) OVER (PARTITION BY dims)` to source SQL |\n| EXCLUDE (non-nested) | `WINDOW_MEASURE`  | Add YAML window measure with `range: all`              |\n| Nested (LOD in LOD)  | classify          | Apply Nested LOD Decision Tree below; route or SKIP    |\n| INCLUDE              | `SKIP`            | Document in top-level `comment:` field with reason     |\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n**Classification (run first on every LOD):**\n\n- `INCLUDE` → `SKIP` (no Databricks equivalent)\n- Nested (LOD inside LOD) → apply Nested LOD Decision Tree below\n- `EXCLUDE` → `WINDOW_MEASURE`\n- `FIXED` / `TABLE_SCOPED` → `SOURCE_SQL_OVER`\n\n**Common checks (all LOD calcs):**\n\n- Formula contains `[Parameters.` → SKIP: \"Parameter reference in LOD\"\n\n**`SOURCE_SQL_OVER` checks:**\n\n- Inner aggregation is PERCENTILE → SKIP: \"PERCENTILE not supported in OVER()\"\n- Formula wraps LOD in SUM/AVG → check SUM/AVG Outer Safety (below)\n- Inner expression references another calculation by name → resolve calc chain (below)\n\n**Nested LOD checks:** see Nested LOD Decision Tree below.\n\n**Default:** If uncertain about any LOD → SKIP (safe default)\n\n---\n\n## SOURCE_SQL_OVER — Templates\n\nAlways expose `_lod_` columns via `MAX` or `ANY_VALUE` — never SUM or AVG. OVER() replicates values across rows; SUM/AVG on replicated rows inflates results.\n\n### Grand Total (TABLE_SCOPED or FIXED with empty dims)\n\n**Tableau:** `{FIXED : SUM([Sales])}` or `{SUM([Sales])}`\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER () AS _lod_grand_total\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n\ndimensions:\n  - name: grand_total\n    expr: _lod_grand_total # if role=dimension\n\nmeasures:\n  - name: grand_total\n    expr: MAX(_lod_grand_total) # if role=measure\n```\n\n### Per-Dimension (FIXED with dims)\n\n**Tableau:** `{FIXED [Region] : SUM([Sales])}`\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER (PARTITION BY region) AS _lod_region_total\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n\ndimensions:\n  - name: region_total\n    expr: _lod_region_total # if role=dimension\n\nmeasures:\n  - name: region_total\n    expr: MAX(_lod_region_total) # if role=measure\n```\n\n### Percent of Total\n\n**Tableau:** `SUM([Sales]) / {FIXED : SUM([Sales])}`\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER () AS _lod_grand_total\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n\nmeasures:\n  - name: total_sales\n    expr: SUM(sales)\n  - name: grand_total\n    expr: MAX(_lod_grand_total)\n  - name: pct_of_total\n    expr: SUM(sales) / NULLIF(MAX(_lod_grand_total), 0)\n```\n\n### COUNTD in Source SQL\n\n`COUNT(DISTINCT x) OVER()` is blocked in Spark. Use the `COLLECT_SET` workaround:\n\n**Tableau:** `{FIXED [Region] : COUNTD([Customer ID])}`\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *,\n    ARRAY_SIZE(COLLECT_SET(customer_id) OVER (PARTITION BY region)) AS _lod_region_customers\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n```\n\n### Custom SQL Datasource (CTE wrapping)\n\nWhen the datasource already has custom SQL (`has_custom_sql: true`), wrap the original SQL as a CTE:\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  WITH _base AS (\n    -- original custom SQL here\n    SELECT ... FROM ...\n  )\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER (PARTITION BY region) AS _lod_region_total\n  FROM _base\n```\n\n### Multi-LOD Combination\n\nMultiple FIXED LODs from the same datasource combine in a single source SQL SELECT:\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *,\n    SUM(sales) OVER () AS _lod_grand_total,\n    SUM(sales) OVER (PARTITION BY region) AS _lod_region_total,\n    MIN(order_date) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id) AS _lod_first_order\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n```\n\nPrefix all pre-computed columns with `_lod_` to avoid name collisions.\n\n---\n\n## WINDOW_MEASURE — Templates\n\n### Single-Dim EXCLUDE\n\n**Tableau:** `{EXCLUDE [Quarter] : SUM([Sales])}`\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: sales_excl_quarter\n    expr: SUM(sales)\n    window:\n      - order: quarter\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\nThe `order` field references a **dimension name** (not a SQL column).\n\n### Multi-Dim EXCLUDE\n\n**Tableau:** `{EXCLUDE [Category], [Quarter] : SUM([Sales])}`\n\nOne window entry per excluded dimension:\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: sales_excl_cat_and_qtr\n    expr: SUM(sales)\n    window:\n      - order: category\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n      - order: quarter\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\n### COUNTD in Window Measure\n\n`COUNT(DISTINCT x)` works **natively** in YAML window measure `expr` — no `COLLECT_SET` workaround needed (unlike source SQL OVER):\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: distinct_customers_excl_region\n    expr: COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id)\n    window:\n      - order: region\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\n### Conditional EXCLUDE\n\n`SUM(CASE WHEN ...)` works in window measure `expr`:\n\n```yaml\nmeasures:\n  - name: tech_sales_excl_quarter\n    expr: SUM(CASE WHEN category = 'Tech' THEN sales ELSE 0 END)\n    window:\n      - order: quarter\n        range: all\n        semiadditive: last\n```\n\n### EXCLUDE Filter Caveat\n\nEXCLUDE window measures on metric view datasets are **filter-insensitive**. Dashboard field filters do NOT affect window measure values. This diverges from Tableau where EXCLUDE respects dimension filters.\n\nFor most use cases (percent-of-parent, static subtotals) this doesn't matter. Document in YAML comment when filter interaction is relevant:\n\n```yaml\n# NOTE: sales_excl_quarter is filter-insensitive on MV datasets.\n# Dashboard filters on quarter will NOT recalculate this value.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Nested LOD Decision Tree\n\nWhen you identify a nested LOD (an LOD expression containing another LOD inside its body), apply this tree:\n\n1. **Formula has `[Parameters.`** → SKIP\n\n2. **Any nesting involving INCLUDE** (search for `INCLUDE` between any `{` `}` pair) → SKIP: \"No Databricks equivalent for INCLUDE\"\n\n3. **Outer aggregation wrapping nested FIXED:**\n   - `MAX({FIXED ...})` or `MIN({FIXED ...})` → **migratable** via CTE decomposition (idempotent)\n   - `SUM({FIXED ...})` or `AVG({FIXED ...})` → **SKIP**: row duplication gives wrong values\n   - Check intermediate aggregations between nesting levels too — any SUM/AVG/COUNT between `}` and `{` means SKIP\n\n4. **FIXED + EXCLUDE coexistence** (independent LODs in same datasource, not one inside the other):\n   - Both mechanisms coexist in the same metric view\n   - Source SQL OVER for FIXED + YAML window measures for EXCLUDE\n\n5. **EXCLUDE inner referencing FIXED pre-computed column:**\n   - Simple reference to `_lod_` column in window measure expr → migratable\n   - Complex conditional wrapping (e.g., `COUNTD(IF ... {FIXED} ... THEN ...)`) → SKIP\n\n6. **Triple+ nesting** → SKIP unless all outer layers are MAX/MIN (agent judgment)\n\n7. **Uncertain** → SKIP (safe default)\n\n### CTE Decomposition Template (for nested FIXED with MAX/MIN outer)\n\n**Tableau:** `MAX({FIXED [Customer ID] : SUM([Sales])})`\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  WITH _inner_lod AS (\n    SELECT customer_id, SUM(sales) AS customer_total\n    FROM catalog.schema.orders\n    GROUP BY customer_id\n  )\n  SELECT o.*,\n    il.customer_total AS _lod_customer_total\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders o\n  LEFT JOIN _inner_lod il ON o.customer_id = il.customer_id\n\nmeasures:\n  - name: max_customer_total\n    expr: MAX(_lod_customer_total)\n```\n\n**Why MAX/MIN works but AVG/SUM doesn't:** The LEFT JOIN replicates the CTE value across all rows for that customer. `MAX` of identical repeated values = the value itself (idempotent). `AVG` counts duplicated rows → wrong denominator. `SUM` sums duplicated rows → inflated.\n\n---\n\n## SUM/AVG Outer Aggregation Safety\n\nWhen the Tableau formula wraps a FIXED LOD in SUM or AVG (e.g., `SUM({FIXED [callid]: MIN([Revenue])})`):\n\n1. Inspect worksheet shelves in the XML (`<rows>` / `<cols>` under each `<worksheet>`) to enumerate the dimensions on rows and columns.\n2. If ALL FIXED dims appear in worksheet dimensions → `MAX` is safe (values are identical within each group, so SUM of identical values = the value)\n3. If FIXED dims ⊄ worksheet dimensions → SKIP and document in the top-level `comment:` field:\n   ```yaml\n   comment: |\n     Skipped calculations:\n     - SKIPPED: revenue_ratio; Reason: SUM/AVG outer on FIXED LOD at coarser viz grain — values would differ from Tableau; Original: SUM({FIXED [callid]: MIN([Revenue])})\n   ```\n4. If uncertain about worksheet dimensions → SKIP\n\n---\n\n## Calc Chain Resolution\n\nWhen the FIXED inner expression is a `[Calculation_X]` or field reference rather than a direct aggregate:\n\n1. Locate the referenced calculation in the workbook XML (search for its caption to find the `<column>` definition, then read the `<calculation>` body).\n2. If the referenced calc is itself an LOD → treat as nested LOD (apply nesting rules)\n3. If the referenced calc is a simple aggregate (SUM, MAX, MIN, etc.) → substitute it in the OVER():\n   ```\n   LOD: {FIXED [date],[center],[dept] : [Calculation_X]}\n   [Calculation_X] = MAX([hours_required])\n   → Resolution: MAX(hours_required) OVER (PARTITION BY date, center, dept)\n   ```\n4. If the referenced calc is a row-level expression (no aggregate) → wrap in appropriate AGG for OVER()\n5. If the referenced calc cannot be resolved → SKIP\n\n---\n\n## Join Interaction\n\nWhen building source SQL with OVER(), check the parent table for each FIXED dimension (use the column → parent-table map you built from `<columns>` ownership when extracting joins — see `xml_extraction.md`):\n\n### Scenario A: FIXED dims from fact table (common)\n\nAdd OVER() directly to source SQL. `joins:` section is unaffected:\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER (PARTITION BY order_date) AS _lod_daily_total\n  FROM catalog.schema.orders\n\njoins: # unaffected\n  - name: customer\n    source: catalog.schema.customers\n    on: source.customer_id = customer.id\n```\n\n### Scenario B: FIXED dims from dimension table\n\nAbsorb the needed join into a source CTE:\n\n```yaml\nsource: |\n  WITH _joined AS (\n    SELECT o.*, c.segment\n    FROM catalog.schema.orders o\n    JOIN catalog.schema.customers c ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id\n  )\n  SELECT *, SUM(sales) OVER (PARTITION BY segment) AS _lod_segment_total\n  FROM _joined\n\njoins: # customer absorbed into CTE; remaining joins stay\n  - name: product\n    source: catalog.schema.products\n    on: source.product_id = product.id\n```\n\n### Scenario C: TABLE_SCOPED / Grand total\n\n`OVER()` with no PARTITION BY always works regardless of joins. `joins:` unaffected.\n\n### EXCLUDE + Joins\n\nNo interaction. EXCLUDE window measures reference dimension **names**, not SQL columns.\n\n---\n\n## Function Translation\n\n| Tableau                      | Databricks SQL                         | Context                         |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `DATETRUNC('week', [field])` | `DATE_TRUNC('week', field)`            | PARTITION BY                    |\n| `YEAR([field])`              | `YEAR(field)`                          | PARTITION BY                    |\n| `MONTH([field])`             | `MONTH(field)`                         | PARTITION BY                    |\n| `IFNULL(LOD, 0)`             | `IFNULL(MAX(_lod_col), 0)`             | measure expr (key: wrap in MAX) |\n| `ZN(LOD)`                    | `IFNULL(MAX(_lod_col), 0)`             | measure expr (key: wrap in MAX) |\n| `INT(LOD)`                   | `CAST(MAX(_lod_col) AS INT)`           | measure expr                    |\n| `IF ... THEN ... END`        | `CASE WHEN ... THEN ... END`           | any expr                        |\n| `COUNTD([x])`                | `ARRAY_SIZE(COLLECT_SET(x) OVER(...))` | source SQL OVER only            |\n| `COUNTD([x])`                | `COUNT(DISTINCT x)`                    | window measure expr             |\n\n---\n\n## Row Duplication Warning\n\nWhen source SQL uses JOINs + OVER(), be careful: LEFT JOIN replicates pre-computed values across all matching rows. Only MAX/MIN outer aggregation is safe on replicated rows. SUM/AVG will inflate values.\n\n---\n\n## Field Exposure Rule\n\nEvery `_lod_` column added to source SQL MUST be exposed as a named dimension or measure in the YAML `dimensions:` or `measures:` array. The dashboard pipeline only sees named fields — raw source SQL columns are invisible to the dashboard agent.\n\n---\n\n## Filter Semantics\n\n| LOD Type | Tableau                    | Databricks MV                              | Match?  |\n| -------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------- |\n| FIXED    | Ignores dimension filters  | Source SQL OVER ignores dashboard filters  | YES     |\n| FIXED    | Respects context filters   | Only if WHERE in source SQL (compile-time) | PARTIAL |\n| EXCLUDE  | Respects dimension filters | Window measures ignore dashboard filters   | NO      |\n| INCLUDE  | Respects dimension filters | N/A                                        | N/A     |\n\nThree filter mechanisms exist in metric views. Each interacts differently with LOD:\n\n| Mechanism              | Affects FIXED OVER? | Affects EXCLUDE window?                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| WHERE in source SQL    | YES                 | N/A (source is table ref for window measures)               |\n| YAML `filter:` field   | NO                  | YES — restricts all data globally before window computation |\n| Dashboard field filter | NO                  | NO                                                          |\n"}}]);
